**Amendment (Storage identity admission)** · `amend:identity:storage-admission` As adoption data under (`gate:identity:implementation`) and (`req:identity:admission-record`), pn-host owns two identities at its durable public-input boundary. Payload constructors produce pn-host/storage-payload/v1, consumed by append, load, rebuild and replay, to detect substitution or damage to the complete canonical stored package. Recognition construction also produces pn-host/recognition-disclosure/v1, consumed by stored-recognition lookup and replay, to distinguish complete validated disclosures that may share a recognized prefix. Neither identity promotes recognition to settlement. No parent identity already supplies either durable binding. Direct byte equality still decides same-edition idempotence and conflict; digests never replace that exact comparison. The assurance class is semantic computational equality under SHA-256 collision and second-preimage resistance.

