**Amendment (Proposal admission)** · `amend:identity:act-proposal-admission` Under (`req:identity:admission-record`), pn-act-profile/act-proposal/v1 is semantic over the exact typed tuple (B,N,Y,D), produced by the Actor through pn-act-profile. The present consumer proposal_matches_supplied_commitment recomputes and compares P with a supplied recorded proposal (portion{``ver:handshake:pre-commitment``; recomputation of the supplied proposal pre-commitment}). It detects substitution across the earlier Actor-proposal boundary, which later host-salted residues cannot establish. Its two private intermediates are SHA-256 of F(r,PN-content-pre-v1,[I,N,Y]) and F(r,PN-dependency-pre-v1,[I,N,D]); P is SHA-256 of F(r,PN-act-proposal-v1,[B,content_pre_digest,dependency_pre_digest]). Neither intermediate is retained or published: the host recomputes both at proposal to check P. The verified header publishes B, P and its Actor signature, and both host-salted commitments (network-v0.31.1, ``def:graph:verified-act`` and ``def:graph:proposal-pre-commitment``). The released ``subsec:deployment:concealment-entropy`` states that P has no host salt and that the pre-digests are not retained after reduction. Any holder of that record can jointly search nonce, payload and dependency list against P; concealment therefore depends on the Actor nonce's entropy. A field-by-field search requires a private pre-digest, held only by the host at proposal, and adds nothing to that host's existing access. B keeps exact authored integer pairs by records' structural equality: 1/2 and 2/4 remain different authored inputs. Hidden fields are Y and D, conditional on the Actor's published nonce specification and the computational-hiding assumption of (`amend:identity:act-concealment`). The host sees N at proposal to recompute both intermediates, then custodies and removes it with the payload. Matching P establishes no Actor authenticity, genuine anchor, entropy, valid signature or information-theoretic hiding. realizes{``subsec:deployment:concealment-entropy``; The Actor nonce and proposal format is specified here; the particular excluded entropy premise is named separately.} realizes{``amend:identity:act-concealment``; The Actor nonce and proposal format uses the declared construction; the particular hiding premise is named separately.} relies{``case:deployment:concealment-entropy-client-generated``; Proposal hiding depends on actual Actor nonce entropy and private handling.}

