**Amendment (Dependency admission)** · `amend:identity:act-dependency-admission` Under (`req:identity:admission-record`), pn-act-profile/act-dependency/v1 is semantic over the exact typed tuple (I,P,S_D,D), produced by the host through pn-act-profile. The present consumer dependencies_match_supplied_commitment decides whether the supplied complete opening matches this supplied retained residue after dependency tombstoning; no empty replacement or unavailable earlier list supplies that decision. C_D is SHA-256 of F(r,PN-dependency-v1,[I,P,S_D,D]), requiring proposal/v1's exact recipe and raw residue. D uses records' strict ActId order, never CBOR string-length order. Hidden field D is concealed in the centralized phase under the same operator-generated salt and custody invariant. Opening deliberately releases the whole list and salt; it restores no carriage and changes no finalized order, recognition or title. Representation and binding refusals reject supplied evidence, while absent, self or later opened dependencies remain host-fault evidence. Matching establishes neither authenticity of P or C_D nor genuine finalized anchors, signatures, entropy or information-theoretic hiding.

**Amendment (Act concealment specification)** · `amend:identity:act-concealment` The computational-hiding assumption is domain-separated SHA-256 with independent unpredictable 256-bit random suffixes, conditioned on B, I, recipe identity, requested states, lengths and other expressly published metadata. Collision resistance alone does not imply hiding. N is exactly u64 big-endian author sequence followed by 32 independently sampled random bytes; its prefix equals I.sequence. The Actor owns durable sequence allocation and saved retry state. The deferred append path checks format and length, freshness against that author's prior nonces and non-reuse across acts. A low-entropy nonce that passes those checkable tests permits any holder of the public record to jointly search N, Y and D against P after reduction. It exposes that Actor's own payload and dependency list to anyone, not another Actor's record, an admission outcome, standing or title. The host-salted content and dependency commitments retain their concealment under the host salts. The pre-digests are neither retained nor published; the host alone recomputes them at proposal, where a field-by-field search adds no access it lacks. This is now explicit as the Actor's own exposure against joint search by any record holder under network-v0.31.1, ``subsec:deployment:concealment-entropy``, ``case:deployment:concealment-entropy-client-generated`` and ``rem:graph:erasure-floor``, read with the public header and deterministic P in ``def:graph:verified-act`` and ``def:graph:proposal-pre-commitment``. Each host salt is exactly u128 big-endian allocation counter followed by 32 independent random bytes. One durable per-run counter covers both roles, reserves before issuance, permits gaps, refuses exhaustion and uncertain rollback, and never retains old secret salts as a non-reuse set. Salt generation remains in pn-host; the pure shared package checks format and equality only (``case:deployment:concealment-entropy-operator-generated``). Production must witness entropy failure, allocation reuse and rollback refusals, custody and removal. Fixed vectors, distinct outputs and these format checks prove none of those duties. Authorized disclosure ends the relevant hiding claim and cannot erase prior recipients' copies. The counter's order and gaps, when disclosed, are permitted metadata. relies{``case:deployment:concealment-entropy-client-generated``; The computational hiding assertion depends on actual private entropy and custody, not merely the published nonce and salt formats.} relies{``case:deployment:concealment-entropy-operator-generated``; The computational hiding assertion depends on actual private entropy and custody, not merely the published nonce and salt formats.} relies{``subsec:deployment:concealment-entropy``; The computational hiding assertion depends on actual private entropy and custody, not merely the published nonce and salt formats.}

